ionally, more subjective language is used for men by the BART model. No other significant differences were observed. However, this relatively broad-brush approach may obscure variation. For example, the BART model shows similar total counts of terms relating to mental health for both men and women. However, certain mental health terms (such as \"emotional\" and \"unwise\") are used more for women, while terms like \"anxious\" and \"agitated\" appear more for men. These word-level differences are examined in the next section.", "bbox": {"x": 839.7, "y": 1448.3, "width": 660.3999999999999, "height": 593.2}}], "ms": 352.91}